@format 1
@id media-loading.in-worklist
@title In Worklist
@section Media loading
@area In Worklist
@entry worklist-relay, delivered-output, tracked-stage-output
@summary Show Worklist paths that load media into program docket state: relay replacement, delivered output placement, and auto-relay stage tracking.
@related media-loading.common.docket-insertion, media-removal.common.docket-removal
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag worklist

@alias roster = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PRoster
@alias list = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PList
@alias docket = Cadroue.Application.LDocket

[worklist-relay] Worklist relay to tab <input>
~ This starts with worklist transfer to tab.
[Technical explanation]
- Require a target Files docket, select the target tab, and read its unlocked entries before inserting the relay media @ roster.PRosterRelaySend(...)
> worklist-target

[delivered-output] Delivered processing output <input>
~ This starts with delivered processing output.
[Technical explanation]
- Resolve the requested destination/original tab and its Files docket in PListDeliveredAdd or PListDeliveredPlace @ list.PListDeliveredAdd(...)
  @ list.PListDeliveredPlace(...)
> delivered-target

[tracked-stage-output] Auto-relay stage output tracking <input>
~ This starts with auto-transfer stage output tracking.
[Technical explanation]
- PListDeliveredTrack resolves the original stage tab and its Files docket before tracking the delivered media path @ list.PListDeliveredTrack(...)
> tracked-target

[worklist-target] Relay target Files available <decision>
~ The program checks transfer target Files available.
[Technical explanation]
- Continue only when the selected target exposes a Files docket @ roster.PRosterRelaySend(...)
? "Target Files docket available" > target-clear-check
? "Target unavailable" > worklist-rejected

[delivered-target] Delivery target Files available <decision>
~ The program checks delivery target Files available.
[Technical explanation]
- Continue only when the destination/original tab still exposes a Files docket @ list.PListDeliveredAdd(...)
  @ list.PListDeliveredPlace(...)
? "Target Files docket available" > delivered-scan
? "Target unavailable" > delivery-rejected

[tracked-target] Tracking target Files available <decision>
~ The program checks tracking target Files available.
[Technical explanation]
- Continue only when the original stage tab still exposes a Files docket @ list.PListDeliveredTrack(...)
? "Target Files docket available" > tracked-scan
? "Target unavailable" > tracked-rejected

[target-clear-check] Existing unlocked target paths <decision>
~ The program checks existing unlocked target paths.
[Technical explanation]
- Read all unlocked target entries before relay insertion @ roster.PRosterRelaySend(...)
? "Unlocked target paths exist" > target-remove
? "Nothing to replace" > target-no-remove

[worklist-rejected] Relay loads nothing <output>
~ This path ends with transfer loads nothing.
[Technical explanation]
= No target media insertion occurs because there is no target Files docket.

[delivered-scan] Scan delivered media <process>
~ This step handles scan delivered media.
[Technical explanation]
- Scan the delivered output with PListMediaScan and pass the accepted result directly to LDocketPathsAdd with the supplied batch and delivered=true @ list.PListMediaScan(...)
  @ docket.LDocketPathsAdd(...)
> map:media-loading.common.docket-insertion

[delivery-rejected] Delivered media loads nowhere <output>
~ This path ends with delivered media loads nowhere.
[Technical explanation]
= No media is inserted because the requested target Files docket is unavailable.

[tracked-scan] Scan and track delivered media <process>
~ This step handles scan and track delivered media.
[Technical explanation]
- Scan the delivered path and call LDocketDeliveredAdd; an absent path is added as delivered+locked, while an existing mismatched/unlocked entry is updated to the supplied batch and locked state @ list.PListDeliveredTrack(...)
  @ list.PListMediaScan(...)
  @ docket.LDocketDeliveredAdd(...)
> tracked-complete

[tracked-rejected] Stage output not tracked <output>
~ This path ends with stage output not tracked.
[Technical explanation]
= No program docket state changes because the original stage Files docket is unavailable.

[target-no-remove] No target removal needed <junction>
> target-clear-join

[target-remove] Remove replaceable target entries first <process>
~ This step handles remove replaceable target entries first.
[Technical explanation]
- Call LDocketPathsRemove for the unlocked target entries before relay insertion; the synchronous removal behavior is covered by Media removal / Docket removal @ roster.PRosterRelaySend(...)
  @ docket.LDocketPathsRemove(...)
> target-clear-join

[tracked-complete] Stage output represented in program docket <output>
~ The produced media is now represented in the program file list.
[Technical explanation]
= When the scan returns supported media and LDocketDeliveredAdd reports a change, the target docket contains or updates a locked delivered entry and raises LDocketChange.

[target-clear-join] Relay replacement paths converge <junction>
> relay-scan

[relay-scan] Scan and insert relay media <process>
~ This step handles scan and insert transfer media.
[Technical explanation]
- Scan relay paths with PListMediaScan, create a new batch, and pass the supported paths directly to LDocketPathsAdd; PListPathsAdd is not called @ list.PListMediaScan(...)
  @ docket.LDocketPathsAdd(...)
> map:media-loading.common.docket-insertion
